WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.000
At Oakland's International

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.400
Mail Center, Customs officers routinely
scrutinize mail from many countries.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:26.040
Today, Customs Officer Naomi is taking a
closer look at a package sent from Kenya.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.280
It’s declared as head lamps,
this is the x-ray image of the package

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.560
and you can see
some inconsistencies there,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.760
so it is really worth opening
and having a look.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:41.560
While these African manufactured
head lamps show organic matter

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.960
inconsistent with the declaration
the packaging itself

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.320
appears sound.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:51.160
According to the Declaration,
it is a headlamp

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.320
and when I push the button

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:57.040
it actually works.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.720
If it's a genuine concealment,
the exporters have gone to some trouble.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:05.080
So it really looks like it's very legit.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.560
Naomi dismantles the torches,
but it's the batteries

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.640
that have piqued her interest.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.120
Once in the x-ray machine, Naomi’s sharp

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.280
eyes immediately
spot a clear inconsistency.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.200
One side is dark, the other side is light.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:23.640
Naomi and her

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.200
colleague Vinodh suit up in the 
exam room as a precaution,

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.800
before cracking open the bogus batteries.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.440
Bingo.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:38.440
And you can see the white powder 
here, this is what’s inside,

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.440
we are going to test it for what
the substance is.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.120
At Auckland International Airport

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:53.560
it’s not unusual for returning Kiwis
to bring home all manner of souvenirs.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.480
Some items could carry biosecurity risks,
so they’re always checked before

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.440
being cleared.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.400
So this passenger
came in a couple of days ago,

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.840
they had declared on their form

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:06.160
and verbally to us
that they had lots of trophy items.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.200
We didn’t know what was 
and wasn’t CITIES items.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.160
CITES is an agreement among 
New Zealand and other nations

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.760
that protects against exploitation
of endangered wild animals.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.040
Department of Conservation rangers

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.400
Jason and Avi
will check over the large consignment.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.800
This quantity is certainly unusual
coming in

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:27.480
with as many trophy mounts
and skins in one go.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.720
Particularly without paper work,
South Africa is generally

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.720
pretty good at issuing paper work.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:34.880
We do have some CITES items

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.040
that we still to have to process here
that the importer is unlikely to get back.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.080
Probably Caracal skull

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.160
which goes with this skin.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:47.600
They’re a medium-sized 
cat, African Savannah.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.520
These needed a permit to come in.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:08:00.000
And finally,
there’s a series of Hippo teeth.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:03.080
So this is the same as ivory

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:06.080
so again, needed documentation
to get those in the country.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.880
The Rangers set to work on over
20 hunting trophies.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.920
There is a skull for the Brown Hyena
and this is the skin from it so

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.080
obviously taken in South Africa

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.760
but it’s not CITES listed so

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.760
the importer can get that back.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:27.360
With DOC confiscating the CITES
items, Biosecurity

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.840
can make their final checks
on the skulls, skins and teeth.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:35.680
Lots of them are nice and clean
and lots of them aren’t, like the skins

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.240
arent, aren’t

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:40.640
tanned they’re just sort of salted
and dried and brought through.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:44.720
And a couple of the skulls
are not particularly clean,

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:48.520
as you can see there is still tissue
in the nasal cavities on that one.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.760
Snappy, snappy.

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:55.760
We get to pack it all up so it’s
nice and safe

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.600
and then send it away
to the treatment company

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.560
so they can treat it so it can be safe
to enter the country without bringing any

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:01.960
diseases in it.

